Create a text Page. For starting content, pass initial_blocks as a JSON array of up to 100 Markdown strings, for example ["# Summary", "First paragraph."]. For an image from chat, leave it out of initial_blocks. Create the Page, attach the image to its page_id with write_page_reference, then insert the returned Markdown. To create at the top level of a Drive Space, pass space_id and omit parent_page_id. Use parent_page_id only for a real Page ID, never a Space ID; the child inherits its Space. Omit Space and parent IDs for a private Page. Any Page can have a top-level coordinator_dot_id (a stable personal or shared Dot profile ID). For idempotency_key, Use a UUID or a string of 1–200 ASCII characters. Allowed characters are letters, digits, periods, underscores, colons, and hyphens. Retain the same valid idempotency_key across retries. Read the selected Space root first when accessible; otherwise read the writable shared parent and pass parent_page_id. For a new Site in a Space, register the Site with Sites first, then create an empty child with its site_project_id, the selected parent_page_id and a retained idempotency_key. Complete attach_site_to_page using the returned metadata.page_id before building. If interrupted, retry with the same Site, Page and key, not replacements. Do not convert the Space root or a document. Use Markdown for inline formatting and links, even inside supported HTML wrappers. Reserve HTML for documented exceptions such as underline and rich table-cell structure. For a table that should wrap or fit the Page, use automatic widths. Reset an existing wide or fixed-width table with edit_page set_block_metadata and metadata:{layout:"normal",tableWidths:null}; preserve explicitly requested sizing. See the write-page catalog (`references/page-content.md#rich-table-cells`) for supported HTML. For a Plan, send namespace=plans, a retained idempotency_key, namespace_properties_schema_version=1, and namespace_properties with a status and optional assignee_account_user_id. This tool is part of plugin `Pages`.

