Create a downloadable, textured 3D model (GLB) from a description or images using Tripo H3.1 (model: tripo3d-h3-1). Use for game props, product models, characters, and objects. Returns 3D geometry and textures in GLB format.

Call whoami first and check availableMeshModels. 3D model generation requires a paid workspace with 3D access; an empty model list is not fixed by switching image/video models. Never promise access from the tool schema alone.

TEXT: pass promptText (up to 1024 characters), with optional negativePrompt. Describe one complete object and its materials.
IMAGES: pass referenceImages with url or taskId of a finished image. Do not include promptText, negativePrompt or imageSeed with images. For multiple views, label them with type: front, left, back, right. Supported sets are front+left, front+left+back, or all four; front+back alone is invalid. One image needs no view label.
ChatGPT uploaded images: pass referenceImageFile directly when provided. Local agents: upload the reference image with init_upload and complete_upload. Reuse Runway image URLs verbatim or use taskId; do not upload them again.

Defaults: standard geometry, standard PBR textures. Costs 20 credits for text or 30 for images; detailed textures add 10 and detailed geometry adds 20. To disable textures set BOTH texture and pbr to false (10 credits for text, 20 for images). faceLimit: Maximum face count: 1,500,000 with standard geometry or 2,000,000 with detailed geometry. autoSize estimates physical scale; it does not establish precise dimensions. GLB is the only output format.

Returns a background task ID. The viewer polls and displays the interactive textured 3D model with orbit/zoom and Download GLB when complete; without a viewer use get_task. Hosts that cannot render 3D retain the still preview and download. Generation typically takes about 3 minutes. Do not resubmit while it is running. This tool does not upload existing GLBs or render 3D models from specified cameras. Do not pass a GLB URL into generate_image/generate_video; those need a rendered 2D image. This tool is part of plugin `Runway`.

