Generate OR edit one or more images with a Runway-hosted model. This is the only image tool — there is no separate "edit_image" tool; pass the source as `referenceImages[0]` to edit it. Model selection, supported ratios, sizes, and reference limits are documented on their input fields.

MODEL STATUS: Call `whoami` before choosing a model. Check `modelDeprecations` for upcoming sunsets and unavailable task variants; warn briefly about a relevant upcoming sunset, and ask before switching models. The model enum lists supported inputs, not current availability.

CREDIT MODE: Runway account availability is checked against the currently connected workspace.

For a creative product ad video from a product URL or image, use `generate_product_marketing_video`; it extracts the product image and builds the ad. If extraction fails, ask for the real product image or screenshot; use a text stand-in only with the user's agreement. For video generation or editing, use `generate_video` for one shot or `generate_multishot_video` for 3–5 connected scenes. To translate an ad's on-screen copy while preserving its layout, use `localize_ad`.

MODEL SELECTION: Select `model` explicitly with the picking heuristic in the `model` field, which covers the full catalog, costs, account gates, and fallbacks; honor a model the user names. In brief: nano-banana-pro for photoreal images and reference-guided edits; the latest available GPT Image for readable in-image text and precise edits; Seedream for many-reference composites; Bria FIBO for licensed-data generation; P-Image or Recraft Flash for low-cost prompt-only drafts; Recraft Vector or GPT Image 2.6 for a vector SVG; GPT Image 2.6 for an animated GIF (see `outputFormat`); a Seedream layers model to split one image into layers. Use `remove_image_background` to cut out an existing image.

MODES:
- New image: pass `promptText` describing one standalone image, without reference images.
- Edit: put the source in `referenceImages[0]` and describe the change. Tag it and refer to that tag in the prompt, for example `@input at sunset`.
- Composite: pass multiple distinctly tagged references and refer to each tag in the prompt, for example `@person standing in @room`.

USER ATTACHMENTS: ChatGPT uploaded images can be passed as `referenceImageFile`; the server imports them. For Claude, Cursor, and local agents, upload an attached image with `init_upload` → curl → `complete_upload` before passing its Runway URL as `referenceImages[].url`.

REUSING ASSETS: For a finished Runway image, pass its task ID as `referenceImages[].taskId`; the server resolves the URL. Pass a `complete_upload` result or other public image URL as `referenceImages[].url`; never re-upload a usable asset. Copy signed URLs verbatim, including the full `_jwt=` token; never retype, shorten, or reconstruct them. If the original URL is unavailable, upload the image again with `init_upload`.

EDIT BUTTON: If the user says "Edit this image" with a Runway task ID, first confirm in one or two sentences and ask what they want changed; do not generate yet. Once they answer, pass `referenceImages: [{taskId: "<id>", tag: "input"}]` (never retype the URL), describe the change in `promptText`, and keep the source ratio when known. Select an available editing model using the picking heuristic; honor any model the user requested.

MULTIPLE IMAGES: Use `count` for separate images, options, or variations. Describe ONE standalone image in `promptText`; omit requested quantities and grid/collage/contact-sheet language unless the user wants one collage. For deliberately different concepts, make separate calls with `count: 1` and a tailored prompt for each.

STYLE SAFETY: Do not use names of artists, directors, photographers, studios, or other living creators as style anchors. Translate a named style into neutral visual descriptors (camera language, palette, lighting, era, texture) before calling the tool.

USER-FACING REPLIES: Choose the model internally. Mention its name only if the user asks which model was used; describe the image content otherwise. This tool is part of plugin `Runway`.

