Generate music from a text description — songs, instrumentals, scores, loops, stings — and return an MP3. Describe genre, mood, instrumentation, tempo, structure, and (for songs) lyrics or vocal style in `promptText`.

CREDIT MODE: Runway account availability is checked against the currently connected workspace.

MODELS (pick with `model`; default `lyria-3-pro`):
- `lyria-3-pro` (8 credits): Full-length music — songs, scores, instrumentals. Use for a complete track or soundtrack.
- `lyria-3-clip` (4 credits): Short music clips — stings, loops, background beds, jingles. Use for intros, transitions, or a bed under a short video.
- `eleven-music-v2.5` (10 credits for the default 30s, 20 per minute, 196 for the 10-minute maximum): Music with an exact length (`durationSeconds`, 3-600 seconds, default 30) and an optional `forceInstrumental` switch. Use when the user needs a specific length or a track up to 10 minutes. Not enabled on every workspace yet.
Lyria output length is fixed per model: use `lyria-3-clip` for short beds/stings and `lyria-3-pro` for a full track. For an exact length, use `eleven-music-v2.5` with `durationSeconds`; its cost grows with the length (ceil(seconds × 196 / 600) credits, minimum 1).

WHEN TO USE:
- "make me a song about…", "write a lo-fi beat", "background music for my video", "an orchestral score that builds", "a 10-second jingle".
- "a 3-minute track", "exactly 45 seconds of music", "a 10-minute ambient bed" → `eleven-music-v2.5` with `durationSeconds`, when `whoami` lists it.
- NOT for speech/voiceover, NOT for sound effects, NOT for adding a soundtrack to an existing video (generate the music here, then combine externally).

PAID PLAN REQUIRED: music generation is not available on free Runway workspaces. On a free workspace this tool returns paid_plan_required without creating a task — follow the NEXT line in that result (`show_plans_and_credits` with `gatedCapability`) and do not retry. If a `whoami` call made for this request returned an empty `availableMusicModels` with `upgradeUrl`, skip this tool and call `show_plans_and_credits` with `{"gatedCapability": "Generating music"}` directly. If the user may have upgraded since an earlier `whoami`, call `whoami` again instead of reusing that result. Tell the user that generating music needs a paid plan rather than naming the model.

