Generate a sound effect from a text description — foley, ambience, impacts, UI sounds, creature noises, whooshes, loops — and return an audio file. Describe the sound source, texture, environment, and how it evolves in `promptText`. With `model: "mirelo-sfx-2"` (Mirelo SFX 2.0) it can also score an existing video: pass `video` and it creates a full sound-effect track that matches the clip.

CREDIT MODE: Runway account availability is checked against the currently connected workspace.

MODELS:
- `sound-effects` (default): text only, MP3, 0.5–30 seconds, optional `loop`. COST: 1 credit per second of requested `duration` (rounded up); 2 credits when `duration` is omitted and the model picks the length. Paid plans only.
- `mirelo-sfx-2`: text to sound effect (0.1–600 seconds, default 5) or video to sound effect (pass `video`; 1 second up to the video length, default the whole video, max 600). Prompts up to 2000 characters, plus `negativePrompt`, `format` (mp3, wav, flac), `seed` and, with a video, `preserveSpeech`. No `loop`. COST: 2 credits per second of `duration` (rounded up, minimum 1), e.g. 10 seconds = 20 credits. Paid plans only, and not yet enabled on every workspace.

WHEN TO USE:
- "a door creaking open", "rain on a tin roof, 10 seconds", "sci-fi laser blast", "a looping crackling campfire", "footsteps on gravel", "a notification chime".
- "add sound effects to this video", "replace the audio of this clip with foley" → `model: "mirelo-sfx-2"` with `video`.
- NOT for music (use `generate_music`), NOT for speech or voiceover (use `generate_speech`).

AVAILABILITY: Sound effects require a paid Runway workspace. Call `whoami` and select a model listed in `availableSoundEffectModels` (empty on free plans). `mirelo-sfx-2` is not enabled on every paid workspace yet. If a call returns `paid_plan_required`, follow its NEXT instruction and do not retry the other model. If a model is rejected as not enabled, tell the user and stop — do not retry that model.

PROMPTING TIPS: name the source first ("heavy wooden door"), then the action ("slams shut"), then the space ("in a stone hallway, long reverb tail"). Mention pacing for longer effects ("starts quiet, builds to a roar"). Set `loop: true` for ambience or beds meant to repeat seamlessly (default model only). For a video, describe which sounds matter ("footsteps and wind, no music"). Max 450 characters on the default model, 2000 on `mirelo-sfx-2`.

REUSING A VIDEO FROM THIS CHAT: if the source is a video a Runway tool generated earlier in this conversation, pass its task ID as `video.taskId` (no `url`, no `videoFile`). The server looks up the URL and duration. Do NOT ask the user to upload or download it.

HANDLING USER ATTACHMENTS (video, `mirelo-sfx-2` only):
- Claude/Cursor/local agents: upload local files first via `init_upload` -> PUT the bytes -> `complete_upload`, then pass the returned asset URL as `video.url`.
- ChatGPT: pass an uploaded video as `videoFile`; the tool imports it server-side. NEVER pass local paths such as `/mnt/data/file.mp4` as `video.url`. Pass the duration alongside it as `video: {durationSeconds}`.

USER-FACING REPLIES: Talk about the sound (what it is, how long, what it's for), not the model or task machinery. Do not mention ElevenLabs or Mirelo unless the user asks. The output is an audio file (an audio track, not a new video) the viewer plays inline; headless agents get the URL from `get_task`.

Parameters:
- model: Optional. `sound-effects` (default) or `mirelo-sfx-2`.
- promptText: Required. What the sound effect should be.
- duration: Optional. Length in seconds. Default model: 0.5–30, omit to let the model choose. `mirelo-sfx-2`: see MODELS. Required with a video whose length is unknown.
- loop: Optional, default model only. true to design the effect to loop seamlessly (ambience, beds). Default false.
- negativePrompt, format, seed: Optional, `mirelo-sfx-2` only.
- video: Optional, `mirelo-sfx-2` only. `{url?, durationSeconds?, taskId?}` — the video to score. URL must be a Runway-hosted `/datasets` URL (from `complete_upload`) or a public HTTPS video URL.
- videoFile: ChatGPT-only uploaded video file param `{download_url, file_id, mime_type, file_name}`.
- preserveSpeech: Optional, with a video only. false to drop the clip's dialogue; it is kept by default.
- name: Optional. Display name for the asset in the user's Runway library. Defaults to the prompt. This tool is part of plugin `Runway`.

