Turn text into spoken audio (text-to-speech) with one of Runway's preset voices and return an MP3. Pass the exact words to speak in `text` and pick a `voice` by name.

CREDIT MODE: Runway account availability is checked against the currently connected workspace.

COST: `eleven_v3` and `eleven_multilingual_v2`: 1 credit per 50 characters of `text`, rounded up (minimum 1), max 5000 characters per call. `eleven_v4`: 2.2 credits per 1,000 characters until October 12, 2026 PT, then 5 credits per 1,000 characters, rounded up (minimum 1), max 2500 characters per call. `eleven_v4_turbo`: 3 credits per 1,000 characters, rounded up (minimum 1), max 2500 characters per call. `fish-drama-3`: 1 credit per 250 characters, rounded up (minimum 1) (provisional), max 5000 characters per call. `seed-audio-1.0`: 5 credits upfront, then 0.25 credits per second of output in total, rounded up (5–30 credits; output is capped at 120 seconds), max 2048 characters per call. Split longer scripts into several calls.

AVAILABILITY: Speech generation requires a paid Runway workspace. Call `whoami` and select a model listed in `availableSpeechModels` for the connected workspace. `eleven_v4_turbo` and `fish-drama-3` are not enabled on every paid workspace yet. If a call returns `paid_plan_required`, follow its NEXT instruction and do not retry another speech model from this schema.

MODELS (pick with `model`, or omit it: the default is `eleven_v4`, falling back to `eleven_v3` on enterprise workspaces and for text over 2500 characters, SSML `<break>` tags or a 3-letter `languageCode`):
- `eleven_v3`: Most expressive. Understands inline delivery tags in the text such as [whispers], [laughs], [sighs], [excited]. Best for dialogue, characters, and emotive narration. Requires a paid workspace.
- `eleven_multilingual_v2`: Steadier and more predictable; ignores delivery tags. Best for long neutral narration, product voiceover, and non-English text. Requires a paid workspace.
- `eleven_v4`: Newest expressive model with inline delivery tags ([laughs], [whispers], [pause]) and a much lower per-character price. Max 2500 characters per call. The only model with multi-speaker `dialogue`; also takes library voices from `search_voices`. Paid plans only; check workspace availability with `whoami`.
- `eleven_v4_turbo`: Faster, cheaper Eleven v4 for high-volume or latency-sensitive narration, with the same inline delivery tags and voices (presets or `search_voices`). Single voice only: no `dialogue`. Max 2500 characters per call. Prefer `eleven_v4` for the most emotive read. Paid plans only, and not yet enabled on every workspace.
- `fish-drama-3`: Fish Audio's expressive drama model. Direct delivery with bracketed cues such as [barely holding it together] or [small laugh], or wrap words in <whisper>...</whisper>. Uses its own seven English voices (see FISH AUDIO VOICES); no voice controls, speed, languageCode, voiceId or dialogue. Max 5000 characters per call. Paid plans only, and not yet enabled on every workspace.
- `seed-audio-1.0`: ByteDance's omni audio model. `text` can be the exact words to speak in its default voice, or a scene description that mixes voice direction, dialogue, music, ambience and sound effects in one clip (up to 2 minutes). No preset voices, voice controls, speed, languageCode, voiceId or dialogue. Max 2048 characters per call. Paid plans only.

VOICES for the Eleven models (pick with `voice`; default `Leslie`). Choose by the user's description ("deep male narrator", "cute cartoon voice", "British woman, calm"); do not ask the user to pick from the full list unless they want to browse:
See the `voice` input description for the full voice profiles.

FISH AUDIO VOICES: `fish-drama-3` only accepts these English voices (default `Sarah`); the voices above do not work with it:
See the `voice` input description for the Fish voice profiles.

WHEN TO USE:
- "read this aloud", "voiceover for my video: …", "narrate this script in a British accent", "say 'welcome back' in a robotic voice".
- "a conversation between a detective and a suspect", "a two-host podcast intro": `eleven_v4` with `dialogue`.
- "lots of short voice lines, fast and cheap": `eleven_v4_turbo` when `whoami` lists it.
- "a radio host talking over upbeat music and crowd noise": `seed-audio-1.0` with the scene described in `text`.
- NOT for music (use `generate_music`), NOT for sound effects (use `generate_sound_effect`), NOT for cloning a specific person's voice, NOT for translating or re-voicing an existing audio/video file.

PROMPTING TIPS: `text` is spoken verbatim — do not include stage directions as plain prose. With `eleven_v3`, `eleven_v4` or `eleven_v4_turbo` you may add bracketed delivery tags inline, e.g. "[whispers] Don't move. [pause] Did you hear that?"; `eleven_multilingual_v2` ignores tags. `eleven_v4` and `eleven_v4_turbo` reject SSML `<break>` tags — use [pause]. Use punctuation and line breaks to control pacing. Set `languageCode` when the text is not English and pronunciation matters. Prefer a 2-letter ISO 639-1 code (`es`, `de`, `pt`) or a 3-letter code for eleven_v3 (`eng`, `fil`). Region aliases such as `pt-BR` are accepted where supported.

USER-FACING REPLIES: Talk about the voiceover (which voice, what it says, how long), not the model or task machinery. Do not mention ElevenLabs unless the user asks. The output is an MP3 the viewer plays inline; headless agents get the URL from `get_task`.

Parameters:
- text: Required unless `dialogue` is given. The words to speak, verbatim (or, for `seed-audio-1.0`, a scene description). Max 5000 characters (2500 for `eleven_v4` and `eleven_v4_turbo`, 2048 for `seed-audio-1.0`).
- voice: Optional. Preset voice name from the profiles in the `voice` input description. Default `Leslie`, or `Sarah` for `fish-drama-3`.
- voiceId: Optional, `eleven_v4` or `eleven_v4_turbo` only. A voice from `search_voices` when no preset fits the user's description.
- dialogue: Optional, `eleven_v4` only. Ordered lines `[{ voice | voiceId, text }]` for a conversation between up to 10 voices in one MP3 (max 2,000 characters in total). Use instead of `text`; lines with the same voice are the same speaker.
- model: Optional. `eleven_v4` (default, expressive, cheaper, max 2500 characters), `eleven_v4_turbo` (faster and cheaper v4, single voice, max 2500 characters), `eleven_v3` (expressive, supports tags, the default's fallback), `eleven_multilingual_v2` (steady), `fish-drama-3` (Fish Audio drama voices, max 5000 characters), or `seed-audio-1.0` (speech or mixed audio scenes in a default voice, max 2048 characters, no `voice`). All require a paid workspace; check `whoami.availableSpeechModels`.
- speed: Optional. 0.7–1.2; 1.0 is normal.
- languageCode: Optional. 2-letter ISO 639-1 code (e.g. `es`, `de`, `pt`) or 3-letter code for eleven_v3 (e.g. `eng`, `fil`). Region aliases such as `pt-BR` are accepted where supported. For `eleven_multilingual_v2`, use one of its 29 supported codes (including `fil`); `vi`, `th`, and `bn` are unsupported. Omit it for automatic detection.
- stability, similarityBoost, style, useSpeakerBoost, seed, previousText, nextText: Optional voice controls (see each parameter); not for `fish-drama-3` or `seed-audio-1.0`. Leave them unset unless the user asks for the effect.
- name: Optional. Display name for the asset in the user's Runway library. Defaults to the text. This tool is part of plugin `Runway`.

