Generate OR edit video: text-to-video with promptText; image-to-video with startFrame/startImageFile; video-to-video edits or restyles with referenceVideo/referenceVideoFile. The model parameter gives the full capability matrix and model selection guide.

MODEL STATUS: Call `whoami` before choosing a model. Check `modelDeprecations` for upcoming sunsets and unavailable variants; warn briefly about a relevant sunset and ask before switching. The `whoami.availableVideoModels` list is authoritative, including enabled models absent from this cached description.

CREDIT MODE: Runway account availability is checked against the currently connected workspace.

PAID PLAN: Every video model requires a paid plan. If paid_plan_required, follow its NEXT line to call `show_plans_and_credits` with gatedCapability; do not retry another video model as a workaround.

MODEL PICKING: seedance-2.5 is the general text/image default; the tool falls back to seedance-2 only for compatible requests if unavailable. seedance-2 is the video-to-video default. Use kling-o3-pro for character/product consistency; kling-3-pro for complex multi-character prompt fidelity; veo-3.1 for photorealism with native audio; gen-4.5 for keyframe storytelling. Pick h3-max only when named by the user. Check the model field for newer model variants, constraints, costs, and fallback rules.

FOOTAGE EDIT ROUTING: Use `edit_video` (Aleph 2.0) for targeted changes that must preserve motion, framing and timing, or when the user names Aleph/Edit Studio. Use `referenceVideo` here for looser motion transfer, restyling or substantial re-imagining. Both require a paid workspace. If one approach changes too much or cannot accept the source, consider the other. This tool can remove/replace backgrounds and objects in footage; see referenceVideo for detailed routing.

For creative product ads from a product URL/image, use `generate_product_marketing_video`. For multi-shot videos driven by one prompt, use `generate_multishot_video`.

For still-image edits, use `generate_image`.

DURATION: Omit duration unless the user asks for a length. Text/image requests target 10s; edits use the known source length. Pass referenceVideo.durationSeconds when known.

4K COST: Only choose 4K when explicitly requested. Kling 4K costs 43 credits/second; Gemini Omni 1.2 Flash 4K costs 21 credits/second; Seedance 2.5 4K costs 110 credits/second plus input-video cost. Vague requests for high quality do not authorize 4K.

ANIMATE: When the user clicks Animate on a finished Runway image, ask what motion they want before generating; then use startFrame.taskId. For ChatGPT uploads, use startImageFile or referenceVideoFile, never /mnt/data paths. Copy signed URLs verbatim, including _jwt.

USER-FACING REPLIES: Do not name the model unless asked. Describe the subject, motion and mood. This tool is part of plugin `Runway`.

