Loads a Runway skill: step-by-step instructions for a creative task that combines several Runway tools.

When the user's request matches a specific skill below, call this before any generation tool and follow the returned instructions instead of generating directly. Load the general `runway` skill only when unsure which tool fits. Skip it when the skill is already loaded in this conversation. Reading a skill is free.

Skills:
- `mood-board`: Create a mood board that sets the visual direction for a project — use when the user asks for a mood board, or wants to see a collection of reference images presented together in a single composed output rather than as separate standalone images.
- `resize-image`: Change an existing image's aspect ratio — resize, reframe, or extend it to a new ratio (like 21:9, 1:1, or 9:16) while keeping the original content intact and filling the new areas with contextually relevant extensions. Not for generating a new image from a description or for cropping content out.
- `runway`: Choose the right Runway tool for a media request — images, video, footage edits, audio, 3D, ads, finishing, or workflows — and handle uploads, references, models, and credits. Use for any Runway request that no more specific Runway skill covers.
- `social-thumbnail`: Create a thumbnail or cover image for social media — a single still designed to grab attention with a readable headline and at most one line of subtext. Not for motion video or multi-shot pieces (use generate_video or generate_multishot_video), nor for plain illustrative stills with no headline or layout intent (use generate_image directly).
- `workflow-builder`: Create, edit, inspect, or run a node-based Runway workflow — a reusable pipeline of generation steps ('build a workflow that makes a 1-minute product ad video', 'a workflow that restyles my static ad with different characters', 'run my workflow'). Use when the deliverable is the reusable workflow itself, or a run of one, not a single hand-orchestrated output. This tool is part of plugin `Runway`.

