Remove the background from a video: SAM3 segmentation tracks the subject you describe across every frame and outputs a .webm video with a TRANSPARENT background (alpha channel) — the subject is kept, everything else is removed. Set `invert: true` to do the opposite: cut the subject OUT and keep the background.

CREDIT MODE: Runway account availability is checked against the currently connected workspace.

WHEN TO USE THIS:
- "remove the background", "cut out the person", "green-screen this video", "isolate the product", "make the background transparent".
- NOT for replacing the background with new content (use `edit_video` — it can restyle or swap backgrounds in place), NOT for content generation (`generate_video`), NOT for sharpening (`upscale_video`).

SOURCE VIDEO CONSTRAINTS: at most 60 seconds (~1800 frames at 30fps). Cost: 1 credit/second of input video. `video.durationSeconds` is REQUIRED — the task is billed by duration and the backend rejects sources without one.

OUTPUT: a .webm file with an alpha channel. Warn the user that some players show transparent regions as black/gray; the transparency is real and works in editors and compositing tools.

AVAILABILITY: account-gated. If the task is rejected with an "Unknown task type" error, this workspace does not have access yet — tell the user the feature isn't enabled for their account instead of retrying.

DEFAULT MODEL (`sam3`): tracks the subject you describe, with the limits above. Pick it to keep a specific object, animal or product, or for `invert`.

AI MEDIAKIT MODELS (optional `model` values):
- `mediakit-matte-portrait` (AI MediaKit Portrait Matting): pick for cutting people out automatically, with no subject prompt. Source: up to 300s, at most 2160px on the short side and 3840px on the long side, no silent HEVC, silent VP9, silent DNxHR. Output: a transparent .webm (alpha channel). Cost: about 30 credits per minute at up to 720p, x1.5 at 1080p, x3 at 2K, x4 at 4K; each task rounds up to whole credits.
MediaKit needs a paid plan and is not enabled on every workspace: only pass one of these models when `whoami` lists it in `availableVideoToolModels.remove_video_background`. On a model_unavailable result, tell the user and offer the default model. Do not retry the MediaKit model.
MediaKit matting takes no `subject` (it is ignored) and rejects `invert` and `keepSound`; it keeps the source audio.

REUSING A VIDEO FROM THIS CHAT: if the source is a video a Runway tool generated earlier in this conversation, pass its task ID as `video.taskId` (no `url`, no `videoFile`). The server looks up the URL and duration. Do NOT ask the user to upload or download it.

